      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm just going to bump this up now that worlds can be seen on our profiles. It would be great if we didn't have to submit worlds we want to share with our friends as public. I think it'd be best implemented as another \"unlisted\" publishing status between \"public\" and \"private\"\n\nThe \"unlisted\" world publishing status could work in a few ways: \n1. Friends could see the world on our social page.\n2. Unlisted worlds could be linked through the VRC website.\n3. Maybe worlds with an unlisted status could be favorited.\n\nBut yeah, if public worlds will be filtered more, this would be a good alternative for world creators.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-16T15:11:58.821Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hopefully I can word this correctly.\n\nI think it'd be a fairly good idea if we were able to somehow allow friends to gain access to our unlisted rooms without needing us to be online to drop a portal.\n\nI know you can use a launch option to do it, but it'd be a really good idea if we were able to grant access to friends and allow them to create instances of our unlisted rooms whilst we are offline.",
